> ## ⚠️ Superseded where it describes hosting or the database
>
> This is generic SaaS boilerplate. Where it conflicts with the Pericles
> doctrine, **the doctrine wins**:
>
> | This rule says | Pericles actually uses |
> |---|---|
> | Backend on Vercel serverless (`@vercel/node` handlers, Edge Functions) | **Coolify** — `backend/` is an Express + socket.io container on port `4112` |
> | Neon serverless PostgreSQL | PostgreSQL (self-hosted / hosted), reached via Prisma |
> | — | **Vercel hosts `frontend/` only** |
>
> The backend cannot be serverless: it holds WebSocket connections
> (`/ws/workflow`) and an in-process position-feed singleton.
>
> Authoritative sources: `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/rules/13-infrastructure.md`,
> `DEPLOYMENT.md`, and the `pericles-tech-stack` skill. Use the
> `coolify-deploy` skill to drive backend deploys.

