  <context description="SaaS Application comprehensive development context">
    This Progressive Web Application serves as a modern SaaS platform with mobile-first design, comprehensive multi-user authentication system, and dual database architecture. The application features real-time search, Google Maps integration, role-based access control, and scalable data management architecture with local Docker development and production Neon serverless deployment.

    Key architectural decisions:
    - React 19.1.0 with TypeScript 5.8.3 for type safety throughout frontend and backend
    - Vite 7.0.4 for modern build tooling and development experience with HMR
    - Tailwind CSS 3.4.17 with modern component system and responsive design
    - Dual database architecture: Local Docker PostgreSQL 16 + Production Neon serverless PostgreSQL
    - Prisma 6.12.0 ORM for type-safe database operations and automated migrations
    - Multi-user authentication with JWT tokens, bcrypt password hashing (12 rounds), and Google OAuth
    - Role-based access control: Owner, Admin, Member, Guest with comprehensive permission system
    - Audit logging and email verification workflow for security compliance
    - Vercel serverless functions (@vercel/node 5.3.7) for scalable API deployment
    - Progressive Web App features for mobile installation with proper viewport and safe area handling
    - Google Maps integration (@googlemaps/js-api-loader 1.16.10) for location-based features
    - Local development: Docker Compose with PostgreSQL 16, pgAdmin 4, and Redis following 500-architecture/517-docker-core-standards-auto.mdc
    - Production database: Neon serverless PostgreSQL following 500-architecture/524-neon-core-standards-auto.mdc
    - Comprehensive Playwright testing infrastructure with accessibility testing (@axe-core/playwright)
    - Application-specific data models and business logic
    - Mobile-first responsive design with modern component styling
    - Environment variable configuration supporting dual database environments

    Development should prioritize mobile user experience, PWA functionality, efficient database operations, security best practices, comprehensive testing coverage, and maintaining modern design aesthetics across both local Docker and production Neon environments.

    Authentication Architecture:
    - Multi-user system with role-based permissions (Owner > Admin > Member > Guest)
    - JWT authentication with access tokens (15min) and refresh tokens (7 days)
    - bcrypt password hashing with 12 rounds and salt generation
    - Google OAuth integration for single sign-on
    - Email verification workflow with approval process
    - Comprehensive audit logging for security events
    - Account lockout protection and session management
    - Test user system for Playwright authentication testing (test@saas-app.com / testpass123)

    Database Architecture:
    - Local Development: Docker PostgreSQL 16 with pgAdmin 4 and Redis for full-stack development
    - Production: Neon serverless PostgreSQL with autoscaling, connection pooling, and database branching
    - Prisma ORM for type-safe operations across both environments
    - Automated database migrations with version control
    - Authentication tables: users, user_sessions, audit_logs, email_queue
    - Application data tables with optimized search indexes
    - Row-Level Security (RLS) policies for multi-tenant applications in production
    - Proper foreign key relationships and constraints
    - Connection pooling optimization for serverless deployment
    - Database seeding with owner and test user accounts
    - Neon branch management for feature development and testing

    Testing Infrastructure:
    - Playwright E2E testing across mobile (Pixel 5, iPhone 12) and desktop (Chrome, Safari)
    - Critical deployment-blocking tests in tests/e2e/critical/
    - Accessibility testing with @axe-core/playwright for WCAG 2.1 AA compliance
    - Authentication testing with test user (test@saas-app.com / testpass123)
    - Visual regression testing and responsive layout testing
    - CI/CD integration with test reports and failure artifacts
    - Docker-based testing environment for consistent local testing

    Deployment and DevOps:
    - Local Development: Docker Compose with secure multi-service orchestration
    - Production: Vercel serverless platform with Neon database integration
    - Environment variable management for dual database setup
    - Automated CI/CD pipeline with GitHub Actions
    - Database migration automation during deployment
    - Neon database branching for feature development
    - Performance monitoring and error tracking
    - PWA optimization for mobile installation
    - Docker security scanning and optimization

    Version Management:
    - Semantic versioning with package.json version synchronization
    - Package.json version MUST always match the latest GitHub release tag
    - AboutComponent dynamically displays version from package.json import
    - Before ANY release, AI MUST ask user for release type (major/minor/patch)
    - Follow complete release process: version bump → commit → tag → GitHub release → Vercel deploy
    - Use semantic versioning: major (breaking changes), minor (new features), patch (bug fixes)
